      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "190 patients with hypothalamic insufficiency were investigated. The character, frequency of various forms of headache as well as its correlation with neuroendocrine emotional motivation and vegetative disorders were analysed. It was found that headache occurred more frequently in patients with hypothalamic insufficiency (66%) than in the whole population (5-20%). This confirms the role of diencephalic disfunction in its genesis. Psychovegetative disturbances were expressed most of all in tension-type headache (TTH). Very likely that some psychoendocrine mechanisms (particularly depression and idiopathic edema) play important role in pathogenesis of TTH. Clinical effect of Lerivon confirms the pathogenetic role of depression in these cases."},
